{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-44322",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "First, we clear the rational expression by multiplying the equation through by $4$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5y+12}{4} & =2y \\\\ 4(\\frac{5y+12}{4}) & =4\\cdot 2y \\\\ \\cancel{4}(\\frac{5y+12}{\\cancel{4}}) & =8y \\\\ 5y+12 & =8y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve the remaining equation using the addition and multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5y+12 & =8y \\\\ 5y+12-5y & =8y-5y \\\\ 12 & =3y \\\\ \\frac{12}{3} & =\\frac{3y}{3} \\\\ 4 & =\\frac{\\cancel{3}y}{\\cancel{3}} \\\\ 4 & =y \\\\ y & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
